Closes Phase 3's implementation. Behind GROK_LHC; six touchpoints, sentinel 6/6.
154 lib + 92 certification + 10 harness + 5 golden tests.

THE DRAIN WAS INVERTED, AND THAT WAS THE HEADLINE DEFECT

Rounds 1-6 built a host-driven drain: SdkMode::Manual plus a 600s
drain-before-compact window that could compact "with partial material". Lee ruled
it architecturally wrong. It was, and the root cause was an upstream brief line
("background drain pumped from on_thread_idle") applied to a host that needs no
pump.

02-domain-design.md:340 is categorical: when a band entry depends on a derivation
that is not ready, COMPACT DOES NOT STOP. It walks a fallback ladder — rendering,
then degraded compression, then a deterministic excerpt, then a gap — and records
every degraded rung in the receipt. Nothing is lost by not waiting: the canonical
event log holds everything and bands are views that upgrade on the next compact.
The reference host (pi-lhc) runs background mode ALWAYS, regardless of caller
config, with one capped drainSettled at dispose.

Repair: SdkMode::Background unconditional, no knob. Deleted
DERIVATION_DRAIN_BEFORE_COMPACT, drain_derivations_before_compact, the
TimedOutFailOpen wait states, the partial-material fail-open, and the pre-compact
work.drain. Restored the capped drainSettled at close — the sole host drain call.

Measured, credentialed, on the production path:

  replace_compact_for_writeback: 369.8s -> 0.5s
  full credentialed G2 test:     379s   -> 12.6s
  ready vs total at compact:     17/17, and 27/27
  first-touch catch-up:          backlog 12 -> 0

Compact now runs ZERO inference. Verified structurally: the port's thread_view/
contains no inference references at all, so the only path was the host drain this
commit deletes.

TWO ERRORS OF MINE, BOTH CAUGHT BY VERIFIERS

The abort-signal bridge I specified spawned an OS thread that waited forever;
success disarmed its guard without cancelling, so every successful compact leaked
a thread (probe: 3 compacts, 3 leaked). Removed entirely — CompactAbortSignal is
already an Arc<AtomicBool> the guard sets directly. Pinned by a test asserting
thread count returns to baseline.

I also asserted the port's compact abort signal had "no callers, inert today".
False — it has three, including one immediately before the snapshot write. That
made signal:None a live correctness gap, not future-proofing. Now wired to the
turn-abort token with the live-read contract preserved.

ABORT INVARIANT RE-POINTED

Background drain continuing after a turn abort is CORRECT, not a leak. The
invariant is: no compact INSTALLS after abort. Two tests were asserting
call-cessation — the wrong property — and were re-pointed.

TEST SEAMS DELETED RATHER THAN PORTED

bad-code-log.md names the class this project hit six times: "isolated permutation
tests that bypass the real entry point" and "special code whose only purpose is to
isolate internal machinery for tests is usually a smell". Removed accordingly:
TokenWatchSampler, the cancel registry, SNAPSHOT_RACY,
set_refresh_binding_racy_for_test, RegistrySnapshot::from_parts_for_test.

G2 DISCHARGED — the checkpoint carried since Chunk 2

Real grok-4.5 inference, a genuinely compacted body (bands=1), all five hard
write-back gates PASS on the credentialed body, B8.3 calibration clean. G2 also
had to be re-pointed twice: it once reported meaningful results while bands=0
(nothing had compacted), and later rejected degraded output that the repaired
design says is valid and receipt-recorded.

DERIVATION LANES

Real inference on grok-4.5 at low thinking, both lanes ruled by Lee.
PromptSmoothing does this on the production path (counting sampler through
replace_compact_for_writeback: was [], now fires). ToolResultSummary cannot reach
the sampler — DERIV-12 forces truncate-fallback because inference clogged the
queue at intake rate. Documented decision, cited, not a defect. First measurement
of grok-4.5 in this role: quality good (0 discards, ratios 0.88-2.83 against a
0.15 floor, identifiers preserved), latency 3-5x the Codex reference
(SmoothPrompt p90 9.1s).

CARRIED, WITH ONE GATE ON REPLACE SPECIFICALLY

Smoothing sometimes EXPANDS a prompt (~2.9x observed) because
SmoothedPromptGuards has no output upper bound. Two harms: an expanding band
displaces real content, and — worse — smoothed_prompt is meant to record what the
USER said, so a model that answers instead of cleaning writes its own words into
the user's turn. In Shadow nothing user-visible is affected; Replace writes that
band into native irreversibly. Treat as a gate on Replace rollout, not on 3B.

Also carried: the host discards the receipt's degraded/gaps signal (now expected
rather than rare, with zero host visibility); "queue settles between turns" is an
artifact of harness waits, not a measured property; first-touch catch-up cost
~57s of real inference for 12 items.

LIVE_RUNBOOK.md is the deliverable: L1-L6, each with setup, commands, expected
output, failure criteria, evidence to retain, and stop/rollback.

Both verifier lanes passed the architecture in separate trees, with briefs that
carried no cross-lane attribution — so agreement here is independence, not
corroboration.

